
This directory is intended for PlatformIO Test Runner and project tests.

Unit Testing is a software testing method by which individual units of
source code, sets of one or more MCU program modules together with associated
control data, usage procedures, and operating procedures, are tested to
determine whether they are fit for use. Unit testing finds problems early
in the development cycle.

More information about PlatformIO Unit Testing:
- https://docs.platformio.org/en/latest/advanced/unit-testing/index.html

Browser regression checks
-------------------------
`ui-regression.cjs` is a host-only Node.js script, separate from PlatformIO Test
Runner. It requires an installed Playwright module and Google Chrome. Run:

    node test/ui-regression.cjs

If Playwright is installed outside normal module resolution, set
`HATCH_PLAYWRIGHT_MODULE` to its absolute module directory before running.
The current workstation's existing module is available at:

    C:/Users/LENOVO/AppData/Roaming/npm/node_modules/@playwright/cli/node_modules/playwright-core

The script serves assets on a temporary loopback port, uses isolated browser
storage and a simulated clock, and mocks every device API. It checks Wi-Fi
scan/connection/forget flows, saved-network one-tap joins, password dialogs,
two batch slots, removal of unchanged sample records, preservation of owned
records, dashboard rendering stability, changed-data updates, and offline
recovery. It also guards against explicit delay/polling
wait loops in the networking source. It does not contact a board, upload files,
energize outputs, test NVS persistence, or establish radio timing guarantees.
